WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.657
We finish the module by returning to the complete RAG workflow.

00:00:05.657 --> 00:00:07.302
Start with documents. Preserve metadata.

00:00:07.302 --> 00:00:12.772
Create chunks. Generate embeddings. Store or index those vectors.

00:00:12.772 --> 00:00:20.972
When a question arrives, embed the query, retrieve the best evidence, build a grounded prompt, generate the answer,

00:00:20.972 --> 00:00:24.336
and show the sources. Then evaluate the system.

00:00:24.863 --> 00:00:28.235
If retrieval is weak, improve retrieval.

00:00:28.235 --> 00:00:35.435
If the correct evidence is present but generation is weak, investigate the prompt and model behavior.

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:40.755
If the system becomes too large for NumPy, move to a vector store.

00:00:40.755 --> 00:00:48.175
The most important takeaway is that the architecture remains understandable even when the tools change.

00:00:48.175 --> 00:00:54.695
You should now be able to replace our student-support dataset with a small collection from your own work and build the

00:00:54.695 --> 00:00:59.675
same pipeline. That is the practical foundation of RAG.
